HUD glyph contrast (game.buttonPrompts=playstation): the main HUD's face symbols read on a
bright background as on a dark one.

The symbols were thin pastel strokes over a translucent base, at the size of the GameCube
letters they replace (the B letter's pane is 8 layout units wide): on a bright wall they faded
into it. twilight-vita now gives the main HUD (archive main2d) its own variant of those symbols,
a little bolder and on a dark backing of their own outline (platform/vita/ui/ps_glyphs.cpp); the
backing is texels of intensity 0, which a layout picture draws in its "black" colour.
recolor_panes therefore sets a symbol's "black" dark and its "white" to full alpha; bases keep
theirs. The pane's own alpha, with which the game fades a button it does not offer, still
applies.

Colours of HUD pictures only: no texture, pane position or game state changes here.

--- a/src/dusk/button_prompts.hpp
+++ b/src/dusk/button_prompts.hpp
@@ -62,7 +62,11 @@
 
 #if TARGET_VITA
 // Pictures whose texture has a HUD colour take it as their "white" (the colour a white texel
-// draws in), keeping its alpha and the "black". Returns how many panes changed.
+// draws in). A base keeps its alpha and its "black". A symbol is drawn at full alpha, and its
+// "black" turns dark: the HUD's symbols carry a dark backing of their own outline, which the
+// layout draws in that colour, so they read on a bright wall as on a dark one. The pane's own
+// alpha (how the game fades a button it does not offer) still applies. Returns how many panes
+// changed.
 inline int recolor_panes(J2DPane* pane) {
     int changed = 0;
     for (J2DPane* child = pane->getFirstChildPane(); child != NULL; child = child->getNextChildPane()) {
@@ -70,10 +74,16 @@
             J2DPicture* picture = static_cast<J2DPicture*>(child);
             const JUTTexture* texture = picture->getTexture(0);
             unsigned rgb = 0;
-            if (texture != NULL && twv_ps_glyph_hud_tint(texture->getTexInfo(), &rgb)) {
+            const int kind = texture != NULL ? twv_ps_glyph_hud_tint(texture->getTexInfo(), &rgb) : 0;
+            if (kind != 0) {
+                const bool symbol = kind == 2;
                 const JUtility::TColor white = picture->getWhite();
-                const JUtility::TColor tint(u8(rgb >> 16), u8(rgb >> 8), u8(rgb), white.a);
-                changed += picture->setBlackWhite(picture->getBlack(), tint) ? 1 : 0;
+                JUtility::TColor black = picture->getBlack();
+                if (symbol) {
+                    black = JUtility::TColor(0x10, 0x10, 0x14, black.a);
+                }
+                const JUtility::TColor tint(u8(rgb >> 16), u8(rgb >> 8), u8(rgb), symbol ? u8(255) : white.a);
+                changed += picture->setBlackWhite(black, tint) ? 1 : 0;
             }
         }
         changed += recolor_panes(child);
